    "title": "Ralph and Elizabeth Pyszkowski: The heavenly promise",
    "text": "How do you describe the place called heaven? Is it the dream vacation that lasts forever? Many songs have been written that attempt this difficult task. Can we know more details than joy unspeakable and never-ending happiness?\nAmazingly, the Bible gives specifics such as measurements of the New Jerusalem. Like a marriage gift for a bride, God has built a massive city for his people (Rev. 21: 10-27). Its foundations are layered with 12 precious stones from jasper to amethyst. Twelve pearl gates connect to jasper walls that form the boundaries. The city built with pure gold looks like transparent glass. Jesus will establish his everlasting kingdom on earth and richly reward the faithful.",
